*.json.bak

# --- Claude Code ephemeral worktrees (Workflow/Agent isolation:"worktree") ---
# Never track: a worktree is its own git repo, so `git add` records it as a dangling
# gitlink (mode 160000) with no matching .gitmodules entry -- every checkout of a repo
# that accidentally committed one prints "fatal: No url found for submodule path ..."
# (harmless warning, but pure noise on every CI job). See
# plans/active/issues/shared_host_home_filesystem_full_2026_07_26.md for the symptom.
.claude/worktrees/

# --- QG sentinels (local-only fingerprints; never committed) ---
/.qg_last_passed_sha
/.qg_content_sentinel
/.qg_ci_green_marker

# --- QG profiler output (opt-in QG_PROFILE=1; local-only, share explicitly via --outdir) ---
.qg_profile/

# --- QG step-result cache (pip-audit/bandit/actionlint content-hash skip cache; local-only) ---
.qg_cache/

# --- Generated artifacts: regenerated on every QG/quickmerge run from tracked SSOTs;
#     tracking them only churns the worktree (item H, cicd_contract_hardening_2026_06_01).
#     SVG/HTML ← docs/repo-management/cicd-pipeline-definition.yaml (generate-cicd-diagram.py)
#     derived-dependency-manifest.json ← all pyproject.toml (generate-derived-manifest.py;
#       every consumer regenerates before reading, so the committed copy was a stale cache)
#     canonical-dependency-manifest.json ← workspace-constraints.toml (the tracked external-deps
#       SSOT; generate_canonical_dependency_manifest.py). Untracked 2026-06-24: run-version-alignment
#       regenerates it before its own check, and check-dependency-alignment.py degrades gracefully when
#       absent (`if CANONICAL_PATH.is_file()` → {}), so the committed copy was only a stale cache that
#       a local `--fix` re-dirtied → jammed slot-cron-ff-pull (operator: stop generating it locally). ---
/docs/repo-management/CI-CD-PIPELINE.svg
/docs/repo-management/CI-CD-PIPELINE.html
/derived-dependency-manifest.json
/canonical-dependency-manifest.json
#     DOC_INDEX.generated.md ← all docs' frontmatter (scripts/docs/gen_doc_index.py; the L0 map, W4).
#       Consumer-side local + deterministic (byte-identical across hosts); regenerated by the FF-pull
#       cron via --stale-check. NEVER committed — a fleet-shared index is a multi-writer contention
#       hotspot, and any dirty generated file jams slot-cron-ff-pull (C2 decision). ---
/DOC_INDEX.generated.md
#     .DOC_INDEX.generated.md.*.tmp ← atomic-write temp sibling (gen_doc_index.py::_atomic_write_text
#       writes here then os.replace()s over the real file). Cleaned up on success/error; only a
#       hard-kill mid-write leaves one behind — ignore it so it can never dirty the tree / jam the cron.
/.DOC_INDEX.generated.md.*.tmp
/DOC_GRAPH.generated.html
/scripts/docs/vendor-cache/
#     DAG SVGs ← workspace-manifest.json (generate_workspace_dag.py / generate_data_flow_dag.py;
#       generators are deterministic — churn is driven by mutable ci_status inside the manifest,
#       so untracking removes it without needing the ci_status sidecar; nothing imports an SVG).
#       Patterns are NOT root-anchored: the canonical DAGs now live under codex/04-architecture/
#       (the old `/WORKSPACE_MANIFEST_DAG.svg` root-anchored rule missed them → they stayed tracked
#       and churned, jamming slot-cron-ff-pull). Match by basename anywhere. (cicd item; 2026-06-06) ---
*_DAG.svg
CANONICAL_DEPENDENCY_MANIFEST.svg

