# Orchestrator backlog regen output — auto-derived from plan checkboxes (regen-authoritative;
# never hand-committed). The harsh-side path was retired + git-rm'd in f9ec6833b
# (harsh_orchestrator retired 2026-05-25, only _agent_pings.md stays); current orchestrator
# code writes ONLY config.backlog_path() = data/config/backlog.yaml (already gitignored in
# agent-orchestrator), so nothing regenerates this path — but a stale untracked leftover can
# linger in a clone and jam FF-pull. Gitignored defensively so it never reads as dirty.
harsh_orchestrator/backlog.yaml

# cursor-configs/settings.json RE-TRACKED 2026-07-23 (was gitignored 2026-07-09 — see git history /
# plans/active/issues/claude_code_settings_symlink_chain_broken_2026_07_23.md for the full story).
# The 2026-07-09 untrack treated a SYMPTOM: personal model/effortLevel edits kept landing in this
# file and tripping slot-cron-ff-pull.sh's dirty-check. The actual ROOT CAUSE was that
# ~/.claude/settings.json was a SYMLINK into this tracked file, so every `/model`/`/effort` switch
# wrote straight into git. That's fixed now — ~/.claude/settings.json is a real, personal,
# never-tracked file (codex/05-infrastructure/claude-code-settings-symlink.md), and
# scripts/workspace/migrate-personal-settings-keys.sh self-heals if a personal key ever leaks back
# in here. With the root cause closed, this file can safely go back to being git-tracked — the
# whole POINT of the team-shared layer (permissions.allow, mcpServers, hooks) is that it should
# sync via `git pull` like everything else, not require a manual per-clone `cp`.

# Parked-WIP recovery notice left by tree-wip-guard.sh — per-checkout, never committed
.parked-wip

# Generated CI/CD workflow catalog (scripts/generate-workflow-catalog.py) — re-derived from the
# live .github/workflows/*.yml every run, exactly the same "regen-authoritative, never
# hand-committed" shape as backlog.yaml above. Was mistakenly tracked (untracked here
# 2026-08-15 after it kept showing up as a dirty-worktree /done rejection across independent
# slot clones — every regen looked like uncommitted work because it WAS uncommitted generated
# output sitting on top of a tracked file). `git rm --cached` in the same commit as this entry;
# still generated locally by anyone who runs the script, just never diffed against git again.
docs/repo-management/CICD-WORKFLOW-CATALOG.md

# Ad-hoc Slack-channel-read diagnostic dumps (scripts/dev/slack-read-channel.py writes
# ./slack-<channel>-<hours>h.json for WHATEVER channel arg was passed, e.g.
# slack-data-pipeline-alerts-720h.json — the old slack-ci-failures-*.json-only pattern missed
# every other channel, which is exactly how one such dump (164MB) got swept into a real commit
# by the orchestrator's dirty-state auto-commit gate on 2026-08-22). Never real tracked content,
# just whatever window an operator/agent happened to pull — same dirty-worktree /done-rejection
# class as the catalog above.
slack-*.json
